        NCIT:C70856,
        NCIT:C82515 ;
    cosmos_bc:definition "A test of lung function, the FEV1 is the volume exhaled during the first second of a forced expiratory maneuver started from the level of total lung capacity. It is the most frequently used index for assessing bronchoconstriction or bronchodilatation." ;
    cosmos_bc:ncitCode "C38084" ;
